            <ArticleTitle>Sacroiliac joint dysfunction and low back pain in school aged children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Back pain is known to be very common in adults, but the prevalence in children is unknown. Furthermore, the prevalence of sacroiliac dysfunction, and its relationship to back pain has not been previously studied. In this study, we found a high percentage of school aged children had sacroiliac dysfunction and low-back pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
